# Citation metadata, Citation File Format 1.2.0.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AI_GO: a guided decision-tree engine in a single HTML file"
abstract: "A guided decision-tree engine for websites, delivered as one HTML file: the adopting institution's content sits above six comment markers, the engine below them. No build step, no dependency, no network request. The engine handles branching, history, session resumption, translation, screen-reader announcements and a fail-closed publication guard; a companion validator page runs the engine of the file it is given, so the publication verdict exists in one place only. It was written for the University of Lausanne questionnaire published as AI_GO."
# The people credited on the published tool. A harvested citation that named
# only the unit would drop the authors of the reasoning the tool carries.
